  "id": "linux-011",
  "title": "Basic Linux Commands - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Linux commands are used to interact with the operating system through the terminal and perform tasks like file management, navigation, and system monitoring. Learning basic Linux commands helps beginners understand how Linux works and use it efficiently for daily tasks.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Helps beginners understand and use the Linux terminal effectively</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Covers commonly used commands for files, directories, and system tasks</span></li><li value=\"3\"><span>Useful for students, developers, and system administrators</span></li><li value=\"4\"><span>Builds a strong foundation for advanced Linux and server management</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"25_basic_linux_commands\" height=\"400\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands.webp 800w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251215175432788822/25_basic_linux_commands-768.webp 768w\" width=\"800\"><figcaption>25 Basic Linux Commands</figcaption></figure><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>If you're looking to set up your own Linux server to practice these commands or host projects, </span><a href=\"https://www.hostg.xyz/aff_c?offer_id=545&amp;aff_id=115172&amp;url_id=2588\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Hostinger</span></a><span> can be a great option. Hostinger provides affordable VPS hosting plans with full Linux support, including popular distributions like Ubuntu, Cent-OS, and Debian. Its VPS hosting offers full root access, scalable resources, and high-performance servers, making it an excellent choice for both beginners and experienced developers looking for reliable and cost-effective hosting solutions.</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>25 Basic Linux commands to help beginners start working with Linux confidently.</span></p><h3 id=\"command-1-ls\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>1. ls </span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-288\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>ls </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to list files and directories present in the current working directory.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Helps users quickly understand directory contents.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ls [options] [directory]</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ls</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"ls\" height=\"125\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-2.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls.webp 1078w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182120174900/ls-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1078\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The ls command lists all the directories and files available in the current working directory.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-1\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>2. pwd</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/devops/devops-125\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>pwd</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display the full path of the current directory.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>pwd</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>pwd</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"pwd\" height=\"91\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-3.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182543866758/pwd-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The pwd command prints the absolute path of the current working directory.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-1-1\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>3. mkdir</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-126\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>mkdir</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to create new directories or folders.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>mkdir directory_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>mkdir GeeksforGeeks</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"mkdir\" height=\"141\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-4.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216182838441180/mkdir-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The mkdir command creates a new directory named GeeksforGeeks.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-3-mkdir\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>4. cd</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-287\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>cd </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to change the current working directory.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Allows navigation between directories.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Moves the user to the home directory when used without arguments.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cd directory_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cd GeeksforGeeks</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"cd\" height=\"72\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-5.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183054827251/cd-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The cd command changes the current working directory to GeeksforGeeks.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-4-cd\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>5. rmdir</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-555\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>rmdir </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to delete empty directories.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>rmdir directory_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>rmdir TestFolder</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"rmdir\" height=\"122\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-6.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183314023526/rmdir-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The rmdir command deletes the empty directory TestFolder.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"13-cat\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>6. cat</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/system-design/system-design-379\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> cat </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to display file contents and combine multiple files.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cat file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cat test.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"cat\" height=\"71\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-7.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028259479/cat-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The cat command displays the content of the file.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-5-rmdir\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>7. cp</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/system-design/system-design-378\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>cp </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to copy files or directories.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cp source destination</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cp file1.txt file2.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"cp\" height=\"177\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-8.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183542955528/cp-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The cp command copies the contents of file1.txt into file2.txt.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>8. mv</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-292\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>mv</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to move or rename files and directories.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>mv old_name new_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>mv old.txt new.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"mv\" height=\"190\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-9.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183725244470/mv-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The mv command renames the file old.txt to new.txt.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-1\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>9. rm</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-293\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>rm</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to delete files permanently.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>rm file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>rm demo.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"rm\" height=\"171\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-10.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216183934533918/rm-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The rm command deletes the file demo.txt.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-2\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>10. uname</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-127\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>uname </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to display system information.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Shows operating system details.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Helps identify the system.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>uname [OPTIONS]</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>uname</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"uname\" height=\"52\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-11.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251216184055619679/uname-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The uname command displays the operating system name.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-3\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>11. locate</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-128\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> locate</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to find files using a database.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>locate file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>locate demo.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"locate\" height=\"55\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-12.png\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate.png 1070w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-100.png 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-200.png 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-300.png 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-660.png 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-768.png 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217152423784996/locate-1024.png 1024w\" width=\"1070\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The locate command shows the path of the searched file.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Requires updatedb database</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-4\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>12. touch</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/os/os-290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>touch</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to create empty files and updates file timestamps.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>touch file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>touch test.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"touch\" height=\"122\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-13.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217120626325281/touch-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The touch command creates an empty file named test.txt.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-5\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>13. ln</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-129\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>ln</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to create links between files.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Supports hard and soft </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-130\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>links</span></a><span>.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ln -s source link_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ln -s file1.txt link1.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"ln\" height=\"90\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-14.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028316009/ln-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The ln command creates a symbolic link.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-7\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>14. clear</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-131\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>clear</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to clear the terminal screen.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>clear</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>clear</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"clear\" height=\"87\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-15.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028159505/clear-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The terminal screen is cleared.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-8\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>15. ps</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-058\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> ps</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display running processes.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Helps monitor system activity.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ps</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>ps</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"ps\" height=\"132\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-16.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028046287/ps-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The ps command displays currently running processes.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>commonly used as \"ps aux\"</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-9\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>16. man</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-132\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>man</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display command manuals.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Explains options and usage of commands</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>man command_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>man ls</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"man\" height=\"58\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-17.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124028003546/man-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"man--ls\" height=\"568\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-18.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027346853/man--ls-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The manual page of the command is displayed.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-10\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>17. grep</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/devops/devops-457\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>grep </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to search text patterns.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Finds specific strings.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Filters output.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>grep \"text\" file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>grep \"Python\" notes.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"image\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-19.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image.webp 1077w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251218105404923552/image-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1077\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The grep command displays matching lines.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-11\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>18. echo</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-133\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>echo</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display text in the terminal.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>echo \"text\"</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>echo \"Hello Linux\"</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"echo\" height=\"44\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-20.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027247625/echo-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The text is printed on the terminal.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-12\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>19. wget</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-134\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>wget</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to download files from the internet using </span><a href=\"#/article/networking/networking-200\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>URL</span></a></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>wget url</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>wget </span><a href=\"\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_new\"><span>http://example.com/file.zip%3C/span&gt;</span></a></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"wget\" height=\"109\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-21.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027153875/wget-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The file is downloaded successfully.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-13\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>20. whoami</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-135\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>whoami</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display the current user.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>whoami</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>whoami</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"whoami\" height=\"60\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-22.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124027046611/whoami-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The current username is displayed.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-14\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>21. sort</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-136\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>sort</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to sort file contents.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>sort file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>sort test.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"sort\" height=\"479\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-23.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026645675/sort-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The file content is displayed in sorted order.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-15\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>22. cal</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-137\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>cal</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display the calendar.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cal</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>cal</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"cal\" height=\"269\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-24.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026374007/cal-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The current month calendar is displayed.</span></p><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-16\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>23. whereis</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-138\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>whereis </span></a><span>command in Linux is used to locate command files.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Shows binary location.</span></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>whereis command_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>whereis ls</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"whereis\" height=\"57\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-25.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026322289/whereis-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The location of the command is displayed.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-17\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>24. df</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The </span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-071\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>df</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to display disk space usage.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>df [options]</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>df -h</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"df\" height=\"197\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-26.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124026155208/df-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Disk usage details are displayed.</span></li></ul><h3 id=\"command-6-cp-18\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>25. wc</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The</span><a href=\"#/article/linux/linux-139\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span> wc</span></a><span> command in Linux is used to count words, lines, and characters.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Syntax:</strong></b></p><pre><span>wc [OPTION] file_name</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Example:</strong></b></p><pre><span>wc test.txt</span></pre><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Output:</strong></b></p><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"wc\" height=\"372\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/linux-011-img-27.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc.webp 1080w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251217124025366836/wc-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1080\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>The number of words in the file is displayed.</span></li></ul></div>",
  "textContent": "Linux commands are used to interact with the operating system through the terminal and perform tasks like file management, navigation, and system monitoring. Learning basic Linux commands helps beginners understand how Linux works and use it efficiently for daily tasks.Helps beginners understand and use the Linux terminal effectivelyCovers commonly used commands for files, directories, and system tasksUseful for students, developers, and system administratorsBuilds a strong foundation for advanced Linux and server management25 Basic Linux CommandsIf you're looking to set up your own Linux server to practice these commands or host projects, Hostinger can be a great option. Hostinger provides affordable VPS hosting plans with full Linux support, including popular distributions like Ubuntu, Cent-OS, and Debian. Its VPS hosting offers full root access, scalable resources, and high-performance servers, making it an excellent choice for both beginners and experienced developers looking for reliable and cost-effective hosting solutions.25 Basic Linux commands to help beginners start working with Linux confidently.1. ls The ls command in Linux is used to list files and directories present in the current working directory.Helps users quickly understand directory contents.Syntax:ls [options] [directory]Example:lsOutput:OutputThe ls command lists all the directories and files available in the current working directory.2. pwdThe pwd command in Linux is used to display the full path of the current directory.Syntax:pwdExample:pwdOutput:OutputThe pwd command prints the absolute path of the current working directory.3. mkdirThe mkdir command in Linux is used to create new directories or folders.Syntax:mkdir directory_nameExample:mkdir GeeksforGeeksOutput:OutputThe mkdir command creates a new directory named GeeksforGeeks.4. cdThe cd command in Linux is used to change the current working directory.Allows navigation between directories.Moves the user to the home directory when used without arguments.Syntax:cd directory_nameExample:cd GeeksforGeeksOutput:OutputThe cd command changes the current working directory to GeeksforGeeks.5. rmdirThe rmdir command in Linux is used to delete empty directories.Syntax:rmdir directory_nameExample:rmdir TestFolderOutput:OutputThe rmdir command deletes the empty directory TestFolder.6. catThe cat command in Linux is used to display file contents and combine multiple files.Syntax:cat file_nameExample:cat test.txtOutput:OutputThe cat command displays the content of the file.7. cpThe cp command in Linux is used to copy files or directories.Syntax:cp source destinationExample:cp file1.txt file2.txtOutput:OutputThe cp command copies the contents of file1.txt into file2.txt.8. mvThe mv command in Linux is used to move or rename files and directories.Syntax:mv old_name new_nameExample:mv old.txt new.txtOutput:OutputThe mv command renames the file old.txt to new.txt.9. rmThe rm command in Linux is used to delete files permanently.Syntax:rm file_nameExample:rm demo.txtOutput:OutputThe rm command deletes the file demo.txt.10. unameThe uname command in Linux is used to display system information.Shows operating system details.Helps identify the system.Syntax:uname [OPTIONS]Example:unameOutput:OutputThe uname command displays the operating system name.11. locateThe locate command in Linux is used to find files using a database.Syntax:locate file_nameExample:locate demo.txtOutput:OutputThe locate command shows the path of the searched file.Requires updatedb database12. touchThe touch command in Linux is used to create empty files and updates file timestamps.Syntax:touch file_nameExample:touch test.txtOutput:OutputThe touch command creates an empty file named test.txt.13. lnThe ln command in Linux is used to create links between files.Supports hard and soft links.Syntax:ln -s source link_nameExample:ln -s file1.txt link1.txtOutput:OutputThe ln command creates a symbolic link.14. clearThe clear command in Linux is used to clear the terminal screen.Syntax:clearExample:clearOutput:OutputThe terminal screen is cleared.15. psThe ps command in Linux is used to display running processes.Helps monitor system activity.Syntax:psExample:psOutput:OutputThe ps command displays currently running processes.commonly used as \"ps aux\"16. manThe man command in Linux is used to display command manuals.Explains options and usage of commandsSyntax:man command_nameExample:man lsOutput:OutputOutputThe manual page of the command is displayed.17. grepThe grep command in Linux is used to search text patterns.Finds specific strings.Filters output.Syntax:grep \"text\" file_nameExample:grep \"Python\" notes.txtOutput:OutputThe grep command displays matching lines.18. echoThe echo command in Linux is used to display text in the terminal.Syntax:echo \"text\"Example:echo \"Hello Linux\"Output:OutputThe text is printed on the terminal.19. wgetThe wget command in Linux is used to download files from the internet using URLSyntax:wget urlExample:wget http://example.com/file.zip%3C/span>Output:OutputThe file is downloaded successfully.20. whoamiThe whoami command in Linux is used to display the current user.Syntax:whoamiExample:whoamiOutput:OutputThe current username is displayed.21. sortThe sort command in Linux is used to sort file contents.Syntax:sort file_nameExample:sort test.txtOutput:OutputThe file content is displayed in sorted order.22. calThe cal command in Linux is used to display the calendar.Syntax:calExample:calOutput:OutputThe current month calendar is displayed.23. whereisThe whereis command in Linux is used to locate command files.Shows binary location.Syntax:whereis command_nameExample:whereis lsOutput:OutputThe location of the command is displayed.24. dfThe df command in Linux is used to display disk space usage.Syntax:df [options]Example:df -hOutput:OutputDisk usage details are displayed.25. wcThe wc command in Linux is used to count words, lines, and characters.Syntax:wc [OPTION] file_nameExample:wc test.txtOutput:OutputThe number of words in the file is displayed.",
